 "sources": {
  "al": "Pure Al is ASM machinability group E ('needs optimum tool design and machine settings to control chip and finish'); Sandvik: uncoated and PCD grades first, positive sharp edges, built-up edge worst at low speed; Haas starts wrought Al at 490 m/min with its HTSU10 insert (Haas turning-insert speeds and feeds). Drilling, boring and parting speeds here are conservative choices for MQL rather than flood (est.)",
  "cu": "German Copper Institute (DKI i.18, 2010): Cu-OFE C10100 machinability 20 (free-cutting brass 100), chip breaker recommended; carbide turning 220/160/120 m/min at chip thickness 0.1/0.32/0.8 mm; solid-carbide drilling 160 m/min at 0.24-0.29 mm/rev for \u00d812-16 mm. Here drilling at 120 m/min and 0.20 mm/rev under MQL, pecking each diameter (est.)",
  "haas": "Haas ST-10: 3437 x 1596 x 2167 mm installed with chip conveyor, 3,585 kg, 44 mm bar, 15 hp, 6,000 rpm, 12-station turret, US$64,995 list (Haas layout drawing 12/2024; Machine Tool Index, verified 2026-10-02); Bar Feeder V2 for bars up to 4 ft, 10-76 mm, footprint 2104 x 1283 mm",
  "ur": "UR12e (the UR10e, renamed in May 2025): 12.5 kg, 1300 mm, US$50,818-52,674 (Universal Robots press release 12 May 2025 and FAQ; distributor listings)",
  "elma": "Elmasonic P 60 H: 5.75 L, 365 x 186 x 271 mm, 37/80 kHz, US$1,999-3,361; Elma's manual: flammable liquids 'max. 1 litre' only in a separate vessel in the water-filled tank",
  "ad": "A&D AD-4212C-301 weighing module: 51 g at 0.1 mg / 320 g at 1 mg, RS-232C, US$6,736.50",
  "price_al": "5N Al: High Purity Aluminum US$475 for \u00d825 x 305 mm (about $1,180/kg) and $2,350 for \u00d8150 x 350 mm (about $144/kg); Advent 99.9995 % (5N5, not 5N) \u00d820 x 500 mm $1,535 (about $3,500/kg)",
  "price_cu": "C10100 3/4 in round, ASTM B187: Southern Copper $194.53 for 72 in (4.644 kg), about $42/kg"
 },
